{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f77e39d99b57bc5b75", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Chemical Kinetics - Test 6", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 30, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00e0"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00dd", "title": "Chemistry Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0076", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "Assuming <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi>&#956;g</mi></math> of trace radioactive element <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> with a half life of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math> years is absorbed by a growing tree. The amount of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> remaining in the tree after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> years is_____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#956;g</mi></math>. [Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>30</mn></math>]"}, "options": [{"id": "1c82e8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0077"}, {"id": "69837b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0078"}, {"id": "81ff23", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0079"}, {"id": "e45635", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f007a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f007b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "For the reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the rate constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math> (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) is given by<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>47</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfrac></math><br />The energy of activation in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is&nbsp;________ . (Nearest integer)<br />[Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"}, "options": [{"id": "13c1cd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f007c"}, {"id": "fdeb51", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f007d"}, {"id": "e9683c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f007e"}, {"id": "462a86", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f007f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0080", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "Consider the following first order gas phase reaction at constant temperature\n\\(\\mathrm{A}(\\mathrm{g}) \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{~B}(\\mathrm{~g})+\\mathrm{C}(\\mathrm{g})\\)\nIf the total pressure of the gases is found to be 200 torr after \\(23 \\mathrm{sec}\\). and 300 torr upon the complete decomposition of A after a very long time, then the rate constant of the given reaction is ______ \\(\\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}\\) (nearest integer)\n[Given : \\(\\log _{10}(2)=0.301\\)]"}, "options": [{"id": "893129", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0081"}, {"id": "c5495e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0082"}, {"id": "930cce", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0083"}, {"id": "4fa561", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0084"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0085", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "For a reversible reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8652;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>, the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>&nbsp;forward reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The activation energy of the uncatalyzed forward reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. When the reaction is catalysed keeping the reactant concentration same, the rate of the catalysed forward reaction at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>27</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;is found to be same as that of the uncatalyzed reaction at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>327</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The activation energy of the catalysed backward reaction is _______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "e5c00e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0086"}, {"id": "ad60d0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0087"}, {"id": "fce1a2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0088"}, {"id": "502123", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0089"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f008a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "The ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>14</mn></mmultiscripts><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>12</mn></mmultiscripts></mfrac></math> in a piece of wood is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math> part that of atmosphere. If half life of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>14</mn></mmultiscripts></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5730</mn></math> years, the age of wood sample is ..... years."}, "options": [{"id": "1c69fe", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f008b"}, {"id": "b549c5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f008c"}, {"id": "5aed33", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f008d"}, {"id": "a58a29", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f008e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f008f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "The rate constant of a reaction increases by five times on increase in temperature from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>52</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The value of activation energy in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is&nbsp;___ .(Rounded-off to the nearest integer) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "e40062", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0090"}, {"id": "0df28d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0091"}, {"id": "63d04f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0092"}, {"id": "fc1beb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0093"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0094", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the first order reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp; the half life is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math>. The time taken for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>75</mn><mo>%</mo></math> completion of the reaction is mm. (Nearest integer)</p><p>Given :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3010</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4771</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6989</mn></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "47b3dd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0095"}, {"id": "f36a09", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0096"}, {"id": "64fd9f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0097"}, {"id": "459f79", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0098"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f0099", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "<p>The equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>12</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>26000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is followed for the decomposition of compound&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.&nbsp;The activation energy for the reaction is ____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.&nbsp;[nearest integer]</p><p>(Given:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "cfa563", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f009a"}, {"id": "69a76b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f009b"}, {"id": "a8a99b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f009c"}, {"id": "3b43b9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f009d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f009e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "For the given first order reaction&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;the half life of the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3010</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math>. The ratio of the initial concentration of reactant to the concentration of reactant at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math> will be equal to _____.&nbsp;(Nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "77c087", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f009f"}, {"id": "02e2d0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00a0"}, {"id": "7f8a72", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00a1"}, {"id": "99b499", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00a2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00a3", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "The first order rate constant for the decomposition of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>700</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and activation energy is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>209</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Its rate constant (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is (Nearest integer)<br />[Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>79</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>62</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "c45b1f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00a4"}, {"id": "9db95b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00a5"}, {"id": "7af33d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00a6"}, {"id": "84b76a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00a7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00a8", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>87</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;is the time required for the reaction to undergo <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>87</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math> completion and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>50</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is the time required for the reaction to undergo <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math> completion. The relation between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>87</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>50</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;for a first order reaction is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>87</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>50</mn></msub></math><br />The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;(Nearest integer)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e843d1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00a9"}, {"id": "9bdacb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00aa"}, {"id": "e3eab5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00ab"}, {"id": "15d984", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00ac"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00ad", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "For a reaction taking place in three steps at same temperature, overall rate constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfrac></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Ea</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Ea</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Ea</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math> respectively, the overall <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ea</mi></math> is _________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "27791f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00ae"}, {"id": "4d66cd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00af"}, {"id": "f9a504", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00b0"}, {"id": "fb49da", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00b1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00b2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>In the above first order reaction the concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> reduces from initial concentration&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn></math> minutes at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The rate constant for the reaction at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is __________.</p><p>[Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6989</mn></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "9084fb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00b3"}, {"id": "6328a0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00b4"}, {"id": "c9d1b7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00b5"}, {"id": "1c0691", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00b6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00b7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "It has been found that for a chemical reaction with rise in temperature by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> the rate constant gets doubled. Assuming a reaction to be occurring at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, the value of activation energy is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. [nearest integer] (Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>30</mn></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "fe00ee", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00b8"}, {"id": "0c1495", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00b9"}, {"id": "7e51c1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00ba"}, {"id": "194aa9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00bb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00bc", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "Consider the following single step reaction in gas phase at constant temperature.\n\\(2 \\mathrm{~A}_{(\\mathrm{g})}+\\mathrm{B}_{(\\mathrm{g})} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}_{(\\mathrm{g})}\\)\nThe initial rate of the reaction is recorded as \\(\\mathrm{r}_1\\) when the reaction starts with \\(1.5 \\mathrm{~atm}\\) pressure of \\(\\mathrm{A}\\) and \\(0.7 \\mathrm{~atm}\\) pressure of \\(\\mathrm{B}\\). After some time, the rate \\(\\mathrm{r}_2\\) is recorded when the pressure of \\(\\mathrm{C}\\) becomes \\(0.5 \\mathrm{~atm}\\). The ratio \\(\\mathrm{r}_1: \\mathrm{r}_2\\) is ______ \\(\\times 10^{-1}\\). (Nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "2f412b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00bd"}, {"id": "104b16", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00be"}, {"id": "5d2c8b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00bf"}, {"id": "94c31d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00c0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00c1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "The activation energy of one of the reactions in a biochemical process is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>532611</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. When the temperature falls from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>310</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, the change in rate constant observed is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>300</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mrow><mn>310</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></msub></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is<br />[Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"}, "options": [{"id": "53423b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00c2"}, {"id": "141b3c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00c3"}, {"id": "4fcbe5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00c4"}, {"id": "3a8cb3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00c5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00c6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "<p>The number of incorrect statement/s from the following is ______________</p><p>A. The successive half lives of zero order reactions decreases with time.</p><p>B. A substance appearing as reactant in the chemical equation may not affect the rate of reaction</p><p>C. Order and molecularity of a chemical reaction can be a fractional number</p><p>D. The rate constant units of zero and second order reaction are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>molL</mi><mmultiscripts><mo>&#160;</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> respectively</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "77daa7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00c7"}, {"id": "311500", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00c8"}, {"id": "9c3ff7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00c9"}, {"id": "45cb57", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00ca"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00cb", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "<p>The rate constant for a first order reaction is given by the following equation :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>lnk</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>The Activation energy for the reaction is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (In Nearest integer) (Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "1ebe03", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00cc"}, {"id": "e4af97", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00cd"}, {"id": "5cb8ce", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00ce"}, {"id": "0d887a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00cf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00d0", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f6"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5660"], "question": {"text": "The inactivation rate of a viral preparation is proportional to the amount of virus. In the first minute after preparation, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the virus is inactivated. The rate constant for viral inactivation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> (Nearest integer) [Use : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>477</mn></math>&nbsp;property of logarithm<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mrow><mo>:</mo><mi>log</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>log</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "8128b5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00d1"}, {"id": "773614", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00d2"}, {"id": "4d5a1a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00d3"}, {"id": "8fbfe1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00d4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00d5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b479d"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4793"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f2c"], "question": {"text": "Catalyst A reduces the activation energy for a reaction by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The ratio of rate constants, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Catalysed</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Uncatalysed</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&nbsp;is____[nearest integer] [Assume that the pre-exponential factor is same in both the cases. Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"}, "options": [{"id": "de0137", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00d6"}, {"id": "6ef392", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00d7"}, {"id": "b50866", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00d8"}, {"id": "5fb18b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef3c677dc36a88f00d9"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "lin